    {
      "source": "Doctors of Running",
      "priority": 3,
      "url": "https://www.doctorsofrunning.com/2025/06/brooks-ghost-17-review-2025.html",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: Full-length nitrogen-infused DNA LOFT v3 is described as cushioned (not max-soft), with added 2 mm forefoot stack improving underfoot comfort; heel-to-forefoot transition feels smooth with a posterolateral heel bevel and mildly/moderately flexible forefoot.",
        "Responsiveness: The ride is repeatedly called peppy/snappy and nimble, with enough energy return to handle both easy runs and uptempo efforts, though it is not positioned as a top-end fast shoe.",
        "Stability: The platform is mildly stable with a solid midfoot; snug midfoot lockdown plus a firm/stiff heel counter provide strong heel security and lateral control (with possible heel-counter pressure for sensitive runners).",
        "Durability: RoadTack rubber outsole and upper are reported durable, with only minor lateral outsole wear after about 30 miles and an expected average to slightly above-average lifespan."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "Road Trail Run",
      "priority": 4,
      "url": "https://www.roadtrailrun.com/2025/06/brooks-ghost-17-review.html",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: DNA Loft v3 remains soft/light but relatively firm (not mushy), and the higher stack (36.5 mm heel / 26.5 mm forefoot, with +3 mm forefoot) gives noticeably better forefoot softness and impact protection.",
        "Responsiveness: The ride is reasonably dynamic for a daily trainer, with the mellow rocker and 10 mm drop helping smooth roll-through, but energy return is moderate rather than highly bouncy or snappy.",
        "Stability: Though marketed neutral, it has built-in stability from a grounded platform, medial sidewall shaping, sturdier heel counter/collar hold, and outsole geometry that supports centered landings and lateral control.",
        "Durability: The RoadTack rubber outsole is described as sturdy with good road grip, and the more continuous heel/midfoot rubber pattern suggests improved wear resistance and long-term material longevity."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "Believe in the Run",
      "priority": 5,
      "url": "https://believeintherun.com/shoe-reviews/brooks-ghost-17-review/",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "DNA Loft v3 cushioning is balanced (not too soft or too firm) with good underfoot give, and the increased stack (36.5 mm heel / 26.5 mm forefoot) adds impact protection for longer mileage.",
        "Responsiveness is moderate: there is noticeable rebound on toe-off and a slightly bouncy feel, but it is not especially snappy, explosive, or pace-oriented.",
        "Stability is reliable for daily training, with secure lockdown and no reported instability; explicit details on torsional rigidity and heel-counter stiffness are limited.",
        "Durability is a clear positive, with generous outsole rubber and repeated workhorse comments suggesting strong wear resistance over hundreds of miles."
      ]
    }
